<MainLayout title="About InteGrowSys | Fire Safety & Systems Integration" description="Learn about InteGrowSys and its approach to fire and life safety, building systems integration and smart monitoring.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</div><div class="eyebrow">About InteGrowSys</div><h1>Practical safety engineering, thoughtful integration and smarter operations.</h1><p class="lead">We bring fire and life safety systems, building services and monitoring concepts together around the requirements of each site.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container content"><h2>Our approach</h2><p>InteGrowSys works across fire and life safety, planned maintenance, building systems integration and selected security/ELV services. Our focus is to understand the installed systems, the people who operate them and the information needed to respond effectively.</p><h2>Integration before unnecessary replacement</h2><p>Where suitable interfaces are available, an existing system may provide useful status or alarm signals to an additional monitoring layer. Suitability depends on make and model, available outputs, site conditions, network connectivity and the required response workflow.</p><h2>What guides our work</h2><ul class="check-list"><li>Understand the facility and existing equipment before recommending changes.</li><li>Keep approved life-safety operation central to any integration.</li><li>Define which signals, notifications and service records are included.</li><li>Document configuration, limitations and maintenance responsibilities.</li></ul><div class="notice"><strong>Important:</strong> Monitoring add-ons supplement approved life-safety systems; they should not replace required local alarm functions, statutory inspections or emergency procedures.</div></div></section>
</MainLayout>
